  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_639d6fc2ae254164880857f498837b09",
      "statement": "The RateLimits segment (src/segment/rate_limits.rs) renders Claude Code's 5-hour and 7-day rate-limit windows into a single statusline segment, returning true from render (via the Segment trait) iff anything was emitted; limit_sync.rs optionally shares the highest usage seen across sessions on a host.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/limit_sync.rs#L1-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:55db50c3f7c22e26c44a5a78d02b6120071029d7d0a85318e0d0c6c36087bd46:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/rate_limits.rs#L62-L93",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:082301b64d2f1cdc73462a7f4cab2abae7a2ca3580ad759f300a3f4309a6f05d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fe868dc5e8c744cab3a3a31fe1b10534",
      "statement": "The input model defines RateLimits with two optional Window fields, five_hour and seven_day, each carrying used_percentage (a Coerce<f64> that can exceed 100) and resets_at (a Unix epoch in seconds); numeric fields are wrapped in Coerce so a wrong-typed or unparseable value degrades to None instead of aborting the whole parse.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/model/input.rs#L60-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c659eed3fccc3c4ae44fe517e74829bc39be8fb2abeb4ade809a6a19e499d314:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_665b0f9f92fd4885a4b25c80212d97e6",
      "statement": "The weekly window is joined to the 5-hour window by SegmentWriter::window_gap(), a dim-colored glyph (theme.dim + style.window_gap) that is lighter than the composer's inter-segment separator so the pair reads as one grouped segment rather than a boundary.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/render/writer.rs#L144-L154",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dd9838e8de797c398ce8c61d0aad93c56d1ee8dce954af03a336d9263699eded:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/rate_limits.rs#L83-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e02bf65bf208a25d8981472d2e326030b0266e0c8c128aff524ecda3856175b5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2e9fed56b2c240d2b465a7c3d025235a",
      "statement": "Each window body (write_window) is an icon followed by a colored progress bar and percentage: icon() + bar_pct() which emits the bar, a space, and '<pct>%' in the given color; the 5-hour window uses the clock glyph and the weekly window uses the weekly glyph. A reset countdown is appended via write_reset_value as ' ' + reset icon + ' ' + formatted value in theme.reset.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/render/writer.rs#L138-L142",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:acd9d49dc51474e0df6558e374d09a6712d2aebd315cbc95cb4b3d195d43a240:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/rate_limits.rs#L178-L183",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b02197a3f7cffa0a90e68506bc5c45aaa05d55acb67be9a846458c1d378c95d8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/rate_limits.rs#L56-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1127f9b6182357bcb45b57bd72351a2ff70e9af3850732a6fe482a6ba1eb42d4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_214f05b82f9a49c4a830dbb2523bfbe4",
      "statement": "pct_in_range rounds a percentage and accepts it only when the rounded result lands in 0..=999; the upper bound rejects a leaked epoch timestamp (e.g. used_percentage of 1900000000) while still allowing over-limit values above 100, and this check is applied in both the 5-hour and weekly render paths.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/rate_limits.rs#L152-L152",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:88ef3d0e1ca49fc0afa89bd706a35501b11c145b04de4f9f7fbd3c2eeda51097:"
        },
        {
