    },
    {
      "id": "claim_102c6a35b94342bb8f1f947444722b5d",
      "statement": "Cross-session sync is opt-in via Thresholds.limit_sync (default false). In effective_5h/effective_7d, when enabled the session's own (pct, reset) snapshot is recorded into the shared store, then the shared high-water mark is preferred when its reset is in the future; otherwise the session's own values are used. For the weekly window only sessions whose usage crosses weekly_show_at contribute to the store.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/model/config.rs#L124-L125",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4e444fe95b84899e233ff254dedaa24f9f23e344be6a6dc091754c7d9d20759c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/rate_limits.rs#L101-L142",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dfc2283dc35f0ddbec283436f20ba1e86a49e727def89c8c5e8a7f48e742fa02:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_977cbcccdd174594b5bad652730d88e3",
      "statement": "cache_dir() resolves the sync store: $CLAUDEBAR_LIMIT_SYNC_DIR overrides everything (used by tests); otherwise $XDG_CACHE_HOME/claudebar, falling back to ~/.cache/claudebar; it returns None when neither override nor $HOME is set, in which case callers no-op.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/limit_sync.rs#L51-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2e85c67875cdab5045760aafab7123e7c6cf16ba6420e2c8859f9cce6b4f6d23:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e095ce8cba674249a3a1b65d64f71b65",
      "statement": "Per window there is a directory limit-5h.d / limit-7d.d; each record is itself a directory created with atomic mkdir and named '<reset:%010d>_<pct:%07.3f>'. Fixed-width fields make lexical sort match (reset, pct) ordering so the last entry is the highest reset then the highest pct; mkdir is atomic (distinct names for concurrent records, idempotent for identical values), and parse_entry defensively returns None for anything not shaped like the module's own entries.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/limit_sync.rs#L100-L104",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d4f07a64dea77bfa0bd6b1280ef81a25e32a4c8dc79a2f9f96c674a2f9a8e529:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/limit_sync.rs#L66-L85",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1f4136396e5f7af4b1e812fc03ba9367cb0f905113bf057e911881909ce16c67:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_152a048f564f4a7181324f6566412185",
      "statement": "latest() lists the window dir, takes the highest (reset, pct) entry, and rmdirs the rest, keeping the store to a single entry per window so the file count stays bounded across sessions and renders; read and GC errors are swallowed (missing dir yields None, failed rmdir ignored).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/limit_sync.rs#L112-L140",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:50323a5d65a1e9ea2ed5f42e123b45558207e5a46e744b9e90b4f85b311a57ec:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7175e497c8594773a45991acdba3b097",
      "statement": "record() rejects implausibly-far-future resets: the 5-hour window resets at most 6 hours ahead (FIVE_HOUR_MAX_AHEAD_SECS), the 7-day window at most 8 days ahead (SEVEN_DAY_MAX_AHEAD_SECS); it also no-ops for a non-finite or out-of-range pct (outside 0.0..=999.0). All filesystem errors are swallowed because the cache is best-effort and never breaks rendering.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/limit_sync.rs#L42-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77b3a111bcc69e0fb6e4c3d5b68dcd6b45c559d72986f70b3e1af25b6cb88a3f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/limit_sync.rs#L93-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cfee0d0bc50f887548b11b00250ed215552c308069c53e9de416ed91618a3096:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b9b0018e154c48f3a28a36489cd31294",
      "statement": "The segment never breaks rendering: absent fields degrade to None, wrong types are forgiven by Coerce, and render returns false (nothing shown) when neither window has anything to display; the weekly window only appears once pct >= weekly_show_at and is joined by window_gap(); percentages over 999 are never trusted but over-limit values up to 999 still render with crit colors.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/rate_limits.rs#L156-L158",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:200631d3c61ee7bb44260fda15fe1b85c6a442e126ed26194157e2ec1b738ebd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/rate_limits.rs#L261-L269",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bce57fc903b9e168ebe3144f955f2eb5100c8b62ce53e70d816e7717d186aa4f:"
        },
